# textures_views: Views of a normal texture: commandType 7 (a pixel format view), 8 (type, levels and slices) and 27 (with a swizzle). A view is a child resource of its base: a discardable one over a discardable base. The base pages; the views read and write its texels. Listing a view in an exec's resources makes its prepare throw (a fault). A view marked with 52 (setHostValid, clearGuestValid) needs a synchronize, which throws inside opcode 53 and is logged and skipped. 63 discards a view (nothing) and 62 synchronizes and discards it.
